                      [--min-bytes N] [--stop-grace-s S] [--timeout-s S] [-j]

Runs the same code as the resident _sweeper row (aos-sweeper), inside this command, so it
works when that row is paused, stopped or not attached. Only this daemon: the rows on its
table and its default cells (D/procs/*/); child daemons are not entered.

sweep: every row's stderr file of at least --min-bytes is copied into
<stack>/stderr_archives/<UTC>.txt.gz and truncated to 0 (lines written in the last instant
between the final copy and the truncation may be lost). A loop in D/procs/NAME/ that is off
the table but proven alive and started there by this daemon gets {"cmd": "stop"} in its ctl;
a later round, at least --stop-grace-s after that, sends SIGTERM and SIGKILL 10 s later.
Zombies and what it cannot prove are only reported; with the daemon not running no process
is touched. Archives are deleted by age only when --retention-days is given here (the
resident row defaults to 7 days).
--purge: delete every archive the sweeper wrote for this daemon, whatever its age; asks first
on a terminal (-y does not ask). Nothing is archived; no stderr file or process is touched.
--dry-run: print what would be done; no file or process is touched.

Prints one line per action (-j: the round as JSON). Another sweeper working on this daemon:
wait up to --timeout-s seconds (default: 30), then SweepBusy.

flags:
      --purge              delete all archives instead of a round
      --dry-run            only print what would be done
      --retention-days N   also delete archives older than N days (none = no deletion, the default here)
      --min-bytes N        archive stderr files of at least N bytes (default: 1048576)
      --stop-grace-s S     seconds between stop and signals (default: 300)
      --timeout-s S        wait this long for the sweeper lock (default: 30)
  -y, --yes                --purge without asking
  -j, --json               print the round as JSON
  -h, --help               show this help

exit codes: 0 done (findings and warnings included); 1 error (ArgumentsBad, FlagUnknown,
  DaemonMissing, StateMissing, StateBad, SweepBusy).
more: proto8/cmd/aos-sweeper/README.md
""",
